{"id": "EUVD-2026-108740", "enisaUuid": "02e5e252-179e-3f94-810e-04286574fe2b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipv4: stop PMTU walk when nexthop group shrinks\n\nCommit 7d3f3b4367f3 (\"net: ipv4: Cache pmtu for all packet paths if\nmultipath enabled\") made __ip_rt_update_pmtu() update every path.\n\nFor nexthop objects, fib_info_num_path() and fib_info_nhc()\nindependently load nh->nh_grp.  RCU protects each group's lifetime but\ndoes not make the loads observe the same group.  If replacement shrinks\nthe group after the loop accepts an index, fib_info_nhc() returns NULL\nand update_or_create_fnhe() dereferences it.\n\nA deterministic probe only widened the existing window between the real\noperations.  On v7.2, an RTM_NEWNEXTHOP replacement published a\none-member group after the PMTU reader accepted index 1 from a two-member\ngroup, producing:\n\n  KASAN: null-ptr-deref in range [0x0000000000000000-0x0000000000000007]\n  RIP: update_or_create_fnhe+0x45/0x15b0\n\nStop when the indexed path is absent.  Groups are dense, so no later\nindex exists in that snapshot.  The same real-writer window completed\n114,423 PMTU iterations without an oops with this check.  A reproducer\nis available on request.\n\nReplacement requires CAP_NET_ADMIN in the network namespace.  Where\nunprivileged user namespaces are permitted, a local user can obtain it\nin a new user and network namespace.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:23:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:23:17", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7fd60d3c9a1e1b11ef5f1643bbae78d91eae2f4a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c60d17d6dd61adc761ac6f65a008fefbc54cbf87", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c6d670ac656badfd0e15355e07a13a6bdf3b69fd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f27483f9975b5065ff67054cc7eb8edac6083488", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6619e01855e65ef35723685a557e3eb106f4ecf5"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99074"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "10f3997a-27c6-379b-a5af-fa51aee63bb0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3bed2abab4a682d426624ce9add9d7b6d475d4e4 <7fd60d3c9a1e1b11ef5f1643bbae78d91eae2f4a"}, {"id": "1d64ef94-9c24-3a92-8595-2ae32289f4b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7f5005457b3072fe1ddf15bfef869f2a1d98e05e <c60d17d6dd61adc761ac6f65a008fefbc54cbf87"}, {"id": "2af17230-9190-3d5b-8af4-e85f4a5e4ef3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "393091ff-e4ca-3864-ade5-431ec31b8ca9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1.129 <6.2"}, {"id": "4c5d9753-956a-3f5c-9065-2156b1fe8ce8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b1f7bdee5750d6cbb9497140cd6582abc5fdcb9e"}, {"id": "89b670a9-5963-3959-a904-d78d81a6a96e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "8ab39afa-906f-3652-8ccf-25b72344d237", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.79 <6.6.160"}, {"id": "93945bac-5304-3fab-8fc8-ceb997372e36", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "97f4d7cc-9500-3dc0-b4ed-089b1b9601b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7d3f3b4367f315a61fc615e3138f3d320da8c466 <6619e01855e65ef35723685a557e3eb106f4ecf5"}, {"id": "a5589f79-208b-34b3-8682-814e595722d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15.179 <5.16"}, {"id": "aa93202d-3774-3786-b8c9-771d0a64c26d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "c00af157-819a-3de3-a39a-3d20cdb60838", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fc07a232326a623d0be482e307c0